      "titre": "File:Footprints at the Trench (5f00efce-524f-4981-9286-8d2a83af5fa8).JPG",
      "description": "A trench dug-out to demonstrate the sedimentary layers on the side walls. Perspective taken from inside the trench shows footprints found on multiple levels of trench floor. Trenches are a common practice in order to reveal sedimentary layers and estimate timelines. The footprints found at different layers suggest that prehistoric cultures were present over a period of time, as opposed to an isolated event. Keywords: Footprint; Human; Fossil; Trench; Layer; Sediment",
